  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "text_bubble",
      "position": {
        "x": 220,
        "y": -680
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 430,
      "style": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 430
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "title": "API 614 LUBE OIL SYSTEM (LOS)",
        "text": "Demonstrates a heavy-duty API 614 lubrication oil system featuring redundant supply pumps (Main/Auxiliary), oil cooler heat exchanger, duplex filtration with dp monitoring, and pressure control (PRV/BPR) to ensure continuous oil delivery to high-speed turbomachinery bearings.\n\nAfter running, open the Operating Cases Matrix and compare the cold-start, fouled-filter, clogged-filter and failed-open-TCV cases: watch the filter pressure drop and the pump discharge pressure. The pump discharge line runs at about 2.9 m/s.\n\nInstruments: TIT 101 oil supply temperature, PDIT 102 filter pressure drop, PIT 103 header pressure (low alarm / low-low trip) and FIT 104 bearing oil flow. Click Solve all cases in the Measurements tab to see which case trips which alarm.",
        "fontSize": "md",
        "rotation": 0
      }
    },
